  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes checked against live Revit Server 2022 and 2025. History Version/Size, ModelInfo.Size and ServerInfo.Roles map the real server fields (were always 0/null). Lock queries use endpoints that exist (IsModelLockedAsync was always false). RenameFolderAsync with an empty name no longer deletes the folder; DeleteFolderAsync really deletes; Copy/Move/CancelLock/DeleteDescendentLocks report success correctly; 500-after-success of some names is verified. No sync-over-async deadlock (ConfigureAwait(false)); non-ASCII user names are sent percent-encoded; RevitServerApi.Timeout and CancellationToken overloads. RevitServerUiApi throws on HTTP 200 error descriptors and refuses an empty new name. Export checks the destination before downloading, accepts paths with extra separators, and cancels promptly while connecting. RevitServerToolResult.Success is false on an ERROR: line. Several error behaviours changed (exists checks, WalkAsync, lock queries throw instead of returning false); see CHANGES.md.",
